  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The polyhedron is a **cube** since all its faces are squares.\n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a pyramid since a pyramid must have triangular faces (except, possibly, for the base).\n\n- The solid is not a triangular prism because it does not have two triangular bases connected by parallel lines.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-61643\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>The polyhedron is a <strong>cube</strong> since all its faces are squares.</p>\n<p>Also, notice that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The solid is not a pyramid since a pyramid must have triangular faces (except, possibly, for the base). </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The solid is not a triangular prism because it does not have two triangular bases connected by parallel lines.  </p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
